class Solution {
    public int maxProfit(int[] prices) {
        int profit = 0;

        for (int i = 1; i < prices.length; i++) {
            if (prices[i] > prices[i - 1]) {
                profit += prices[i] - prices[i - 1];
            }
        }

        return profit;
    }
}


// explaination 

prices = {7, 1, 5, 3, 6, 4}:

Start (i = 0, price 7): No previous day to compare against, so profit = 0.

Day 1 (i = 1, price 1 vs 7): 1 > 7 is false. Price dropped, so add 0 (profit = 0).

Day 2 (i = 2, price 5 vs 1): 5 > 1 is true. Add 5 - 1 = 4 (profit = 4). Think of buying at 1 and selling at 5.

Day 3 (i = 3, price 3 vs 5): 3 > 5 is false. Price dropped, so add 0 (profit = 4).

Day 4 (i = 4, price 6 vs 3): 6 > 3 is true. Add 6 - 3 = 3 (profit = 7). Think of buying at 3 and selling at 6.

Day 5 (i = 5, price 4 vs 6): 4 > 6 is false. Price dropped, so add 0 (profit = 7).





